  "result": "Summary of VAT implementation:\n\n**`src/invoices.js`**\n- Added `lineVat()` function to calculate VAT per line:\n  - Applies discount first: (lineTotal - discount)\n  - Calculates VAT on discounted amount\n  - Rounds each line's VAT individually using `roundCents()`\n  - Handles missing vatRate by defaulting to 0\n- Updated `invoiceTotals()` to return `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }`\n  - vat = sum of rounded per-line VATs\n  - total = subtotal - discount + vat (clamped at 0)\n- Imported `roundCents` from money.js\n\n**`src/render.js`**\n- Updated `renderInvoiceText()` to display VAT line when present\n- Shows \"VAT: \u20acX.XX\" on its own line just above Total\n- Only displays VAT line if vat > 0 (omits for zero VAT)\n\n**Tests Added (11 new invoice tests)**\n- lineVat calculation with various VAT rates\n- lineVat with discounts applied before VAT\n- lineVat rounding behavior\n- invoiceTotals VAT field inclusion\n- Multiple VAT rates on single invoice\n- Per-line VAT summation\n- Mixed discounts and VAT rates\n\n**Tests Updated (5 render tests)**\n- All updated to include expected VAT in output\n- Added test for omitting VAT line when zero\n\n**Test Results:** 86/86 passing \u2713\n\nThe implementation ensures VAT is calculated per-line with individual rounding, never as a percentage of the invoice total, and all amounts are clamped at zero.",
